      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs have spent the final week of September trimming the fat and sharpening the edges - and that's exactly what a preseason is supposed to look like. <strong>They beat Ottawa 6-1 and 4-2 in back-to-back exhibitions</strong>, a clean sweep that followed the 4-1 loss to Montreal and left Toronto at 2-2 in games that don't count but still reveal plenty. The real story is the roster taking shape around the new faces and the old heavyweights, with the opener against Montreal looming on Tuesday. There's no mystery about the stakes now: a final look at the lines, the last cuts, and the goaltending plan before the games matter. <strong>Watch the opening-night roster and the first real test against the Canadiens on Sept. 29.</strong>",
