        "body": "The season is ending the way too many have for Toronto - with the math gone, the gatekeeper shut, and one last game left to salvage some dignity. <strong>Saturday's 5-1 loss to the Reds</strong> dropped the Blue Jays to 78-83, fifth in the AL East, and set up Sunday's finale with Max Scherzer on the mound at 3:07 p.m. ET - a start that may be his last in a Toronto uniform, though he'll decide that in the offseason. At this point, the club needs more than a farewell tour. It needs a long look at the kids and a harder winter. <strong>Watch the young arms and bats get their late audition, then watch the front office hunt rotation help and offense that can actually carry a lineup</strong>.",
