      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The noise around Toronto's camp is good noise for once - not the usual autumn fog of excuses, but a real test of whether Darko Rajaković can turn optimism into structure. <strong>Zach Lowe's early Coach of the Year buzz for Rajaković has become the loudest note in the building</strong>, and it fits a team that opens preseason Oct. 3 against Miami before the real reckoning arrives Oct. 21 against Chicago. The Raptors are still in training camp, still sorting minutes and pecking order, but that's the point: this is where the rotation gets written in pencil, then erased if someone flashes. The summer chatter has centered on rookies, depth, and who can defend without fouling - the old Toronto problems, dressed up in new jerseys. <strong>What matters next is whether camp can produce a trustworthy second unit and a clearer frontcourt hierarchy before the Heat show up.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
